+## Cinematic documentary mode (v5, default for history / science / true-story narration)
+Use it whenever the story is real (history, medicine, science, true crime) or the user asks for "cinematic", "documentary", "realistic"
+or "Blender". It replaces the "sentence -> object" habit with film-making: a director's storyboard, art-directed sets, motivated light,
+an operated camera and designed transitions. **Read `references/cinematic-standards.md` first** (diagnosis of why v1-v4 looked generic,
+lighting recipes, camera grammar, asset/material standards, render budget, QC). Worked example: `example/forssmann-cinematic/`
+(storyboard.json, film.py, textures.py, post.py, render_all.sh).
+
+Kit (`blender/cinema/`, Blender 5.x Python; in a container `pip install bpy==5.3.0` works when blender.org is blocked):
+`ck.py` (render/colour, procedural PBR library, bevelled/lathe/tube modelling, lights incl. three_point/practical/window/haze, `Shot`
+camera bound to cut markers with eased dolly/track/orbit/crane/rack-focus moves), `human.py` (realistic-proportion humans: garments as
+silhouettes on one rig, sculpted head + expressions, real eyes with lids, fingers, IK with hold/ramp keys, walk/sit/look/talk/breathe),
+`anatomy.py` (ghost figure with skin dissolve, cutaway skeleton, sculpted heart + vessels + beat, venous road, catheter growth,
+road glow, X-ray mode), `props29.py` (1920s rooms with real openings, windows, doors, hospital furniture, surgical lamp, operating table,
+instrument cabinet, X-ray apparatus + light box, desks, books, amphitheatre, stage, modern cath lab).
+
+Stages (each is a gate; do not skip):
+1. **Analyse** - `learn.py brief`; `align.py voice.mp3 script.txt align/` (strip ElevenLabs [tags]; spell numbers); read pauses + tags.
+2. **Storyboard** - write `storyboard.json` (sequences with takeaways; shots with the 10 fields, camera type, lighting setup,
+   transition, word-synced action, continuity block). Gate: `scripts/shotlist_check.py storyboard.json align/words.json` -> `STORYBOARD OK`.
+3. **Prepass** - render any texture that must match the 3D (radiographs, charts) from the same models; generate 2D props with PIL
+   (accurate or unreadable text only).
+4. **Build** - `film.py --set NAME` per set (one set per process, lesson L043). Stills of every shot (`--stills 1A,2B@0.9,...`) at
+   360x640 -> contact sheet (`scripts/contact_sheet.py`) -> fix (generic assets, flat/blown/black frames, camera inside geometry,
+   tangled poses, unreadable action, empty frames) until every panel tells its takeaway. Show the sheet as the storyboard approval.
+5. **Render** - `render_all.sh` (resumable). CPU budget: 540x960, 8 spp + OIDN, `--step 2`; GPU: 1080x1920 every frame.
+6. **Post** - `post.py`: per-shot motion interpolation (never across a cut), per-shot grade (memory sepia, light transitions, fades),
+   upscale + sharpen + grain, captions/supers (ASS), voice over a ducked sound bed, loudnorm -14 LUFS.
+7. **QC + learning** - `scripts/review.py final.mp4 <workdir>`, look at the sheet, `learn.py add/run`, fix the kit, commit `learning/`.
+
